r.LowLatency — THE latency setting, like UE's: 0 = off, 1 = on, 2 = on +
boost. It drives whichever runtime ActiveBackend picks for this GPU;
boost only means something to Reflex and XeLL.

Whether the temporal resolve needs per-object motion vectors (the
Velocity pass) and a jittered projection. Upscalers and TAA need both;
a None passthrough needs neither.

types.doc:
Parallel command recording. Splits a render pass's draw loop across
worker threads: the primary CB opens dynamic rendering with
secondary-buffer contents, each worker records its slice into a
per-chunk secondary CB (redirected transparently via the backend's
per-thread command-buffer override), and EndPass executes the
secondaries in chunk order — the resulting GPU command stream is identical
to the serial loop. The facade routes to the active backend
(IDynamicRHI::Parallel*), which owns the pools and rings.

Usage (caller owns the fan-out; FTaskGraph::ParallelFor over chunk indices):
if (ParallelRecorder::Get().BeginPass(fb, clear, chunks)) {
ParallelFor(chunks, [&](uint32_t c) {
ParallelRecorder::Get().BeginChunk(c);
... Renderer:: draw calls for slice c ...
ParallelRecorder::Get().EndChunk();
ParallelRecorder::Get().EndPass(fb);
} else { ... serial fallback ... }

BeginPass/EndPass run on the recording (main) thread; BeginChunk/EndChunk
run on workers. Nothing may record into the primary between BeginPass and
EndPass. Pools are per-chunk × per-frame-in-flight and live until Shutdown
(driven by Renderer::Shutdown).

